                        "form_id": "880419f3-5ba2-4670-ade8-1db135a50a94",
                        "entry_id": "b62ac280-2315-3345-ab8d-0626326fd3e4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "hétérologiques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c0d0719b-3d6c-3da1-a58c-ceb7b654fd6a",
                        "entry_id": "b62ac280-2315-3345-ab8d-0626326fd3e4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Se dit d’une phrase, d’un syntagme ou d’un mot qui ne se décrit pas lui-même."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f8ce45a-b7ec-4e02-b45f-0c76124e9017",
                                "sense_id": "c0d0719b-3d6c-3da1-a58c-ceb7b654fd6a",
                                "text": "Le mot « long » est hétérologique."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3f850922-fb35-440a-a682-618ac63e54a4",
                        "source_entry_id": "b62ac280-2315-3345-ab8d-0626326fd3e4",
                        "source_sense_id": "c0d0719b-3d6c-3da1-a58c-ceb7b654fd6a",
                        "target_lang_word": "heterological",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "heterological",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "834a1b12-7e89-3513-8c6b-9ef92c36a4be",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb9e8a2-f799-3339-a6d1-fb3829996d95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a word, not describing itself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "643c89d0-9ba0-4075-af70-79652115be3e",
                                                "sense_id": "834a1b12-7e89-3513-8c6b-9ef92c36a4be",
                                                "text": "The words ultrashort and onomatopoeia are heterological: ultrashort might be called short but is not an ultrashort word, and onomatopoeia is not an onomatopoeic word."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24250782-9414-471c-a540-8c8d18f70f02",
                                                "sense_id": "834a1b12-7e89-3513-8c6b-9ef92c36a4be",
                                                "text": "A paradox arises when we ask, \"Is the word 'heterological' heterological.\" If it is, it is not. If it is not, it is."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40025da9-477e-31af-8ddd-19420c26fb25",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb9e8a2-f799-3339-a6d1-fb3829996d95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not true of itself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e73ea53f-8f3c-4681-8776-6a0b8edc09e7",
                                                "sense_id": "40025da9-477e-31af-8ddd-19420c26fb25",
                                                "text": "A further instance of the uncertainty of Prof. Bergmann's views on the subject of negation, is the distinction (considered by him as at least supposable) between \" nicht-richtig \" and \"unrichtig\" (§21,5.). This is done, of course, in order to put a \" heterological \" meaning into his Axiom of Excluded Middle,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca4ee92f-f440-43ee-89ca-57b8d93e9ecd",
                                                "sense_id": "40025da9-477e-31af-8ddd-19420c26fb25",
                                                "text": "It is the dream of a purely heterological thought at its source. A pure thought of pure difference."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d848d90-8edd-4209-b6e4-1a261bde5c78",
                                                "sense_id": "40025da9-477e-31af-8ddd-19420c26fb25",
                                                "text": "But a process philosophy, in order to support a purely heterological thought, has to be capable of doing without subjects steering the process or being steered by it, without substantive names designating 'blocks' in motion, and without points of origin or destination invigilating over a predictable trajectory."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1be7b5d2-3e0d-31f8-82f0-e61e5a35c5ca",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb9e8a2-f799-3339-a6d1-fb3829996d95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not of shared ancestral origin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ad72e60-8156-437b-aec0-94ccdf135e23",
                                                "sense_id": "1be7b5d2-3e0d-31f8-82f0-e61e5a35c5ca",
                                                "text": "The normally situated non-transplanted gonads have the best chance of being able to absorb these substances, for which reason heterological (perhaps also homological) gonads, transplanted on normal organisms, can not get enough of these substances and therefore perish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "496dbaef-469f-4627-b550-987e4a77360e",
                                                "sense_id": "1be7b5d2-3e0d-31f8-82f0-e61e5a35c5ca",
                                                "text": "Growth indices from density and extension of the zones of emigration in explants of rat bone-marrow on addition of various heterological tissue as against the controls."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3003668-1926-367f-9ca2-1a5c6b52a252",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb9e8a2-f799-3339-a6d1-fb3829996d95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Supporting or attracted to otherness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bb94b95-f6bd-45be-a0d8-c86cc343d2dc",
                                                "sense_id": "f3003668-1926-367f-9ca2-1a5c6b52a252",
                                                "text": "That is why it could only have a multitude of names, could only be expressed by the lexical extravagance to which it inevitably leads heterological practice and, as such, does not escape the substitutive discourse. Eroticism is just one of the names of heterological impulse at work — Incomplete through the metonymic effect of the copula — throughout The Caesarean Incomplete."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9bb431c-e62b-47ba-a008-2817086ff964",
                                                "sense_id": "f3003668-1926-367f-9ca2-1a5c6b52a252",
                                                "text": "Bataille's writings in mythical anthropology from the late 1920s already associated the name Sade with a heterological interpretation of erotic expenditure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "410d069b-c335-4aac-8b24-cf1091d32699",
                                                "sense_id": "f3003668-1926-367f-9ca2-1a5c6b52a252",
                                                "text": "This produced a bifurcated narrative of identity as otherness, a heterological trope akin to that we encounter in the ill-defined domain of the Caribbean (Sheller 2003, 2004)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5cc83d7f-130b-328b-b9de-f74baa3a5810",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb9e8a2-f799-3339-a6d1-fb3829996d95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having or supporting multiple interpretations."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41650551-07ae-48be-9802-0cace343c98d",
                                                "sense_id": "5cc83d7f-130b-328b-b9de-f74baa3a5810",
                                                "text": "Indeed, Godzich has situated de Certeau in a heterological tradition, a scholarly tradition in opposition to the hegemonical tradition which has dominated western intellectual thinking. Scholars in the heterological tradition relativise scholarship and point to the constraints enforced by the contemporary social context on the production of truth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bfa5cbbe-1067-4e26-a1e6-ce9c6f3822c9",
                                                "sense_id": "5cc83d7f-130b-328b-b9de-f74baa3a5810",
                                                "text": "Postcolonial theory provides yet another binarity: (ethnic) majority/minority, or imperialistic/ indigenous, yet another aspect of power hierarchy. Therefore I choose in discussions of gender to speak of heterological rather than feminist or queer analysis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a94dc270-476e-4567-be03-cf62b9564e95",
                                                "sense_id": "5cc83d7f-130b-328b-b9de-f74baa3a5810",
                                                "text": "By using this language we can express Yoder's vision of the church as a community that opens up these heterological spaces as partial significations of the coming Kingdom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dc650a5-afb4-4f0d-b79b-f0ee9db732f8",
                                                "sense_id": "5cc83d7f-130b-328b-b9de-f74baa3a5810",
                                                "text": "I will suggest that, if we press the logic of her argument in ways she does not, then either Wyschogrod or God (however named) appears ultimately responsible for training her book's reader in the practice of heterological history."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
